but first we turn our attention to the  southern border  where the growing migrant crisis  continues to spiral out of control  we have brand new numbers from border  patrol tonight 171 000 migrants were  apprehended at the border  in the month of march that's up 60  percent  from february and it's the highest  monthly total in 15 years  even more disturbing the record number  of unaccompanied minors who crossed our  border last month  18 thousand five hundred children that's  seven thousand more than the previous  record for may  in 2019 now we saw how two of those  unaccompanied minors crossed the border  last night  two little girls sisters aged three and  five years old  tossed over a wall left to fend for  themselves  in the middle of a desert miles from  civilization  thankfully the girls are okay here they  are pictured with the hero border agents  who rescued them  el paso sector chief gloria chavez says  she was  horrified by what the coyotes did and  she is looking to hold them accountable  i kneeled down and just wondered as they  were talking to me  what kind of experiences or nightmares  they went through  from ecuador all the way to our border  that we don't even know about  because they were the ones that were  being carried by these ruthless  smugglers  with inhumane treatment of the most  vulnerable population in the world  children those girls are lucky to be  alive  and in this country in one piece others  are not so lucky far too many children  are abused sexually assaulted or  trafficked on their treacherous journeys  through central america  to our border a doctors without border  survey actually found that  31 percent of women and girls and 17  percent of boys  were sexually assaulted on their trips  to america  so familiar are migrant parents with the  assaults on children  that girls are loaded up with birth  control before they embark on their trip  to the cartels these kids are a  commodity no different than the illegal  guns or the drugs they bring into our  country  and for human smugglers business thanks  to joe biden  is booming every day they're making  upwards of  14 million dollars trafficking people  across the border the children who are  stolen into human sex trafficking rings  face a horrifying future from which they  will never  mentally or emotionally recover other  children  don't make it to this country at all  like the nine-year-old girl who drowned  in the rio grande  despite these daily horrors vice  president harris the person who said  we need to get these babies out of cages  and the person tasked  to fix our border crisis has no plans to  visit the border  or hold a formal news conference more  importantly  the biden administration has shown no  indication  that they plan to change their policies  to protect children  who are being used and abused by human  and sex traffickers  until they do this tragedy on the border  will continue
 

